  m_Name: ControllerPitchPropellerData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Controller Pitch Propeller
  engineDescription: A Controllable Pitch Propeller is a marine propulsion system
    that allows the pitch angle of the propeller blades to be adjusted during operation
    to control thrust and vessel speed without necessarily changing the rotational
    speed of the engine. Its main components include the propeller hub, adjustable
    blades, pitch-control mechanism, hydraulic actuator, propeller shaft, control
    valve, bearings, and control system. During operation, engine power is transmitted
    through the propeller shaft to rotate the propeller. The blade pitch is adjusted
    using a hydraulic or mechanical mechanism, allowing the amount of thrust generated
    by the propeller to be varied. Increasing the pitch generally increases the propeller's
    thrust and load, while reducing the pitch decreases thrust and allows efficient
    operation under different vessel conditions. Controllable pitch propellers are
    widely used in ships, tugboats, ferries, offshore vessels, fishing vessels, and
    naval craft. From an engineering perspective, understanding blade hydrodynamics,
    pitch control, thrust generation, cavitation, hydraulic actuation, shaft loading,
    efficiency, vibration, and control-system reliability is essential for efficient
    marine propulsion.
  engineCategory: Engineering
